{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#133","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#133","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#133\",\"parent_revision\":\"342bcfe3e6b1b9433e808cc0ecf06cd5185276cf8a9dc08ec72918398ee4adae\",\"root_revision\":\"342bcfe3e6b1b9433e808cc0ecf06cd5185276cf8a9dc08ec72918398ee4adae\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`scripts/generate_violations_fixture.py` builds `tests/fixtures/benchmark-plugin-violations.zip` with `zipfile.writestr`, which stamps `time.localtime()`. Every run produces a different archive, so the committed fixture can never be checked against what the generator currently emits.\\n\\nThe benchmark workflow extracts the committed archive directly and never runs the generator, so the two drift freely.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What That Drift Already Cost\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe archive went stale twice over and nothing caught it:\\n\\n- 40 of 200 skills carried only FM008 patterns, which stopped matching after commit `5a88d60` inverted the rule. Those skills produced **zero** findings for five months.\\n- FM007 cases still used a `tools:` key that no longer triggers the rule.\\n\\nMeasured at regeneration in #105: the old archive yielded **160** findings, the new one **200**. The benchmark had been passing while measuring 20% less than it claimed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPass a fixed `ZipInfo` date so the archive is byte-deterministic, then have CI assert the committed archive matches a fresh generator run.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #105 \u2014 regenerated the archive and measured the gap\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"8ef476ea3390be8217830036be76304716e1eb76e41dfe847e745f6ace58a061\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-4PA\"}"}